From 146c9f87cd5073087247126a4deb99a2a8565110 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sun, 12 Jul 2026 13:31:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] reaper v1.4.9: USB second factor made binding + AI Advisor
 lock-state UI fix (AI Advisor image)

Make the enrolled USB key a binding third factor: usb_unenroll ("Remove USB key")
now requires the enrolled stick to be physically present (rmcp_usb_find_key), kept
independent of the 'provisioned' code gate so the deprovision-then-unenroll path
cannot strip it either. A holder of the admin login + arming code alone can no longer
remove the USB factor; a lost key can only be cleared by a factory reset / nvram wipe.

Fix the Advisor page lock-state feedback: while a session is armed the page now
re-polls reaper_mcp.cgi?action=status every ~5s, so pulling the USB key (or a session
timeout/disarm) flips the card to "locked" within seconds instead of counting down a
session the router already tore down. (The router-side teardown - fence rule removed +
session file deleted - already fired on key removal; this closes the UI gap.)

One new dict key (RADV_72) in all 25 dict files. httpd/web.c (do_reaper_mcp_cgi,
#ifdef RTCONFIG_REAPER_MCP) + Reaper_Advisor.asp; both images built, noMCP unaffected
(no Advisor).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
